**Spoilers** on the side-effects and on how to kill the shopkeeper follow:

If you kill a peaceful human (such as the shopkeeper, or the oracle, a
vault guard, etc) then you will lose intrinsic telepathy (like what
you got from eating a floating eye). Telepathy is one of the most
powerful intrinsics and losing it can be a real pain (especially on
the later levels, when you are depending on it to avoid those nasty
minotaurs and dragons, and can't seem to find f.e.'s any more).

When killing the shopkeeper, you can get more than one square away and
still hit him with your wand. Remember, fire, cold, magic missile,
lightning wands, among others, are all RAY wands, meaning that they
bounce when they hit a wall. So you just back off to the far end of
the room, and zap the wand diagonally so it hits the shopkeeper after
the ray bounces, and then when he gets mad he'll run straight at you
and you can zap him head on (and often get him twice - both with the
main shot and the backblast). You can hit him 4 or more times before
he even reaches you this way. (Of course if you have a
ring/cloak/potion of invisibility it's even easier because he won't
run after you when he gets mad.)

